3. Defining firewall rules and the repository port
USER PROMPT
What should the domain and repository parts contain?
ASSISTANT GUIDANCE
The domain model was defined around rule type (`ip`, `domain`, or `port`), mode (`blacklist` or `whitelist`), value, numeric ID, and `active`. A `NewFirewallRule` shape omitted the generated ID.
The application port described the storage operations needed by the use cases: read all rules, save a rule, update active status for IDs, and delete rules by IDs. The in-memory adapter implemented that interface with an array and generated sequential IDs.
4. Fixing use-case dependency injection
USER PROMPT
The controller call says: Expected 4 arguments, but got 3. The use case still expects the repository, values, type, and mode. What should I do?
ASSISTANT GUIDANCE
Instead of making the controller pass a repository on every call, the use cases were converted to factories. This preserved the intended dependency direction: Controller → Use Case → Repository.
createAddFirewallRules(repository)
        ↓ returns
addFirewallRules(values, type, mode)
The same factory pattern was then applied to get, delete, and update. The controller received ready-to-run use-case functions through its constructor.
